{"id":"761f22510c77faaf","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-weakly-unbounded.md","title":"Weakly Unbounded","display":"df-weakly-unbounded — Weakly Unbounded","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-weakly-unbounded","aliases":["58-df-weakly-unbounded"],"display":"df-weakly-unbounded — Weakly Unbounded","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-regular.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-unbounded.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-weakly-unbounded"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-weakly-unbounded</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-weakly-unbounded — Weakly Unbounded"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d83de8696e4dad26\" href=\"?note=d83de8696e4dad26\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-regular.md\">../batch16/58-df-regular.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d4c74ee3ac7a06bb\" href=\"?note=d4c74ee3ac7a06bb\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-unbounded.md\">../batch17/58-df-unbounded.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S,\\kappa\\in V\">\\(S,\\kappa\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\subseteq\\kappa\">\\(S\\subseteq\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,\\mathrm{Reg}\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,\\mathrm{Reg}\\subseteq V\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d83de8696e4dad26\" href=\"?note=d83de8696e4dad26\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-regular.md\">../batch16/58-df-regular.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Unbounded}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Unbounded}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d4c74ee3ac7a06bb\" href=\"?note=d4c74ee3ac7a06bb\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-unbounded.md\">../batch17/58-df-unbounded.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WUnbounded}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{WUnbounded}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weakly-unbounded} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{WUnbounded}_S(S,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Reg}(\\kappa)\\land S\\subseteq\\kappa\\land\n\\exists\\alpha&lt;\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Unbounded}_S(S\\cap\\alpha,\\alpha)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weakly-unbounded} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{WUnbounded}_S(S,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Reg}(\\kappa)\\land S\\subseteq\\kappa\\land\n\\exists\\alpha&lt;\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Unbounded}_S(S\\cap\\alpha,\\alpha)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> is weakly unbounded if it is unbounded in some proper initial segment.</li>\n<li>This is weaker than being stationary.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-1","t